ascular, diabetology, asthama, pediatrics, central nervous system, gastro-intestinal, anti-infectives, anti-TB, cephalosporins, and nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug therapies. In addition, it provides chronic therapies, and hospital-based products; products for diabetes and iron supplements for anemia, and a Budesonide-Formoterol combination for asthma. Further, the company is involved in the provision of diagnostics services, and digital healthcare services; and neuro rehabilition business. It operates through network consisting of labs and collection centers. The company has a strategic collaboration with TB Alliance to support the clinical development and commercialization of Telacebec for the treatment of tuberculosis, leprosy, and buruli ulcer. The company was formerly known as Lupin Chemicals Limited and changed its name to Lupin Limited in 2001. Lupin Limited was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Mumbai, India.","beta":0.162,"sharesOutstanding":457293005,"marketCap":903428046848,"trailingPE":17.4092,"forwardPE":20.3686,"priceToBook":3.7554,"enterpriseToEbitda":10.35,"dividendYield":0.91,"heldPercentInsiders":0.4702,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.3529,"earningsGrowth":-0.221,"revenueGrowth":0.111,"website":"https://www.lupin.com","fullTimeEmployees":26021,"recommendationKey":"hold","targetMeanPrice":2290.6667,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":36,"financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":{"0q":{"avg":23.0,"low":20.24,"high":25.76,"yearAgoEps":32.18,"numberOfAnalysts":2.0,"growth":-0.2853,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1q":{"avg":21.785,"low":16.82,"high":26.75,"yearAgoEps":34.75,"numberOfAnalysts":2.0,"growth":-0.3731,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"0y":{"avg":94.4361,"low":88.6813,"high":102.9,"yearAgoEps":128.11,"numberOfAnalysts":33.0,"growth":-0.2629,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1y":{"avg":96.9924,"low":73.2,"high":117.0,"yearAgoEps":94.4361,"numberOfAnalysts":34.0,"growth":0.0271,"currency":"INR","methodolo